Z||000000||JBGehling||01-20-2001||04:28 PM||||Hey, I'm going to look at a garage kept 84 indy pace car fiero tommorow morning. The car has *only* 56,000 miles on it! I was wondering if the car is  in decent condition, if the $4500 they're asking is ok? <BR>Josh||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||01-20-2001||05:56 PM||||You know what they say... The value of something is exactly what someone is willing to give for it...<P>Personally, I wouldn't give that much for an 84. If I was going to spend that kind of money I'd get an 87 or find a deal on an 88. But that is just me. If it is in good shape and worth that to you, go for it! I do love Indys!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||01-20-2001||06:58 PM|||| when i checked prices at Kruse site indys not getting that much $2500 or so inless you love indys i would pass at 4500    ray ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-20-2001||09:47 PM||||If the car is an "excellent" shape I'd think it was worth it. The NIFE price guide shows an Indy in excellent condition and 56K miles is worth $4900.00 That also includes ALL options. Deduct from that missing options, wear, and condition. To pay that much it should look NEW.||||reg||1
